{"id": "12abc7c8-805b-4843-968b-e71d3dae3c01", "sessionId": "25505b9f-a8ea-dd62-6b8d-be45f136b4b6", "turnId": "5093e3ac-9153-41c4-bc70-29af6171bbc2", "inputEntryId": null, "createdAt": 1792605256925, "updatedAt": 1792605256925, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "message", "role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I've just been handed this folder. It's a game somebody else made. That's all I know about it: there's no documentation, and the person who made it isn't around to ask.\n\nHere's what I want to add next, and I'd like a plan for it before anyone writes any code.\n\nKids sign in online and keep their progress.\n- A child should be able to sign in and find their game exactly where they left it, on another device (the family tablet, a laptop at school).\n- The players are children, roughly 8 to 13. They don't have an email address of their own, and a grown-up in the family should be the one who sets them up.\n- Two children of the same family can share one device, each with their own progress.\n- The game must still work for someone who never signs in, and a child who already has progress on this device must not lose it when they first sign in.\n- If the connection drops in the middle of a game, nothing the child did should be lost.\n- It needs a backend and whatever server-side workflows that takes; you decide what those are.\n\nWrite the plan in a file called PLAN.md in this folder. Don't build the feature and don't change any other file.\n\nPLAN.md should have four parts:\n1. How the game works today, as you understand it: what it is, how it's put together, and in detail the parts this feature touches (name the files, functions or components).\n2. The plan: what you would add and change, where, and in what order; the data you'd store and where; how a child signs in; what happens to the progress already on a device; what happens offline; what could go wrong.\n3. What you'd check to know it works.\n4. How you found your way around: what was easy to understand, what was hard, and where you're unsure of what you wrote.\n\nPlease work it out without asking me questions."}], "source": "turn_start", "userDisplayContent": null}
