{"id": "call_83a4b5e90a4b49c9ac9241c0", "sessionId": "25505b9f-a8ea-dd62-6b8d-be45f136b4b6", "turnId": "5093e3ac-9153-41c4-bc70-29af6171bbc2", "inputEntryId": null, "createdAt": 1792605265526, "updatedAt": 1792605265560, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "bash", "detail": {"toolName": "bash", "display": {"summary": "bash: cat /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/CLAUDE.md; echo \"=== SKILLS ===\"; find /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/.claude -type f", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Running", "message": "cat /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/CLAUDE.md; echo \"=== SKILLS ===\"; find /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/.claude -type f", "settledVerb": "Ran", "settledMessage": "cat /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/CLAUDE.md; echo \"=== SKILLS ===\"; find /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/.claude -type f", "statusText": "Running command"}, "kind": "shell", "input": {"command": "cat /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/CLAUDE.md; echo \"=== SKILLS ===\"; find /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/.claude -type f"}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"stdout": "# This folder is for NodeGX apps\n\nIt was set up with `npm create nodegx`. When I ask for an app here, build it as a NodeGX app with the `nodegx`\nserver's tools: `list_projects` and `open_project` for one that exists, `create_project` for a new one. Don't\nwrite a separate web server or hand-written HTML and JavaScript instead: that would be a different app.\n\nWhen the app needs an API key, don't ask me to paste it into the chat. Call `set_function_secret` without a value\nand tell me where to paste it in the project's `.env` file.\n\nTo see an app: `npx @nodegx/preview <the app's folder> --open` — it starts the app's own backend too, when it\nhas one on this computer, so it is also how the app opens again another day.\n\nSome agents never refresh their tool list once a project is open. If a `nodegx` tool you're told about isn't in\nyours, call it through `call_tool` (`describe: true` shows its arguments first).\n\nBuild in small steps: one component at a time, reading each answer before the next. A change the server refuses\nsays exactly what to fix.\n\nTry it the way a person arrives: `drive_page` from the app's start page (leave out `page`) and press through it,\nnot a page opened on its own.\n\nIf I ask for an editor, a viewer or a tool of my own that reads or changes an app here, the guide is the skill\n`nodegx-your-own-editor` (`.claude/skills/nodegx-your-own-editor/SKILL.md`). Read it first; any agent can.\n=== SKILLS ===\n/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/.claude/skills/nodegx-your-own-editor/SKILL.md\n", "stderr": "", "output": "", "truncated": false}, "outputText": "# This folder is for NodeGX apps\n\nIt was set up with `npm create nodegx`. When I ask for an app here, build it as a NodeGX app with the `nodegx`\nserver's tools: `list_projects` and `open_project` for one that exists, `create_project` for a new one. Don't\nwrite a separate web server or hand-written HTML and JavaScript instead: that would be a different app.\n\nWhen the app needs an API key, don't ask me to paste it into the chat. Call `set_function_secret` without a value\nand tell me where to paste it in the project's `.env` file.\n\nTo see an app: `npx @nodegx/preview <the app's folder> --open` — it starts the app's own backend too, when it\nhas one on this computer, so it is also how the app opens again another day.\n\nSome agents never refresh their tool list once a project is open. If a `nodegx` tool you're told about isn't in\nyours, call it through `call_tool` (`describe: true` shows its arguments first).\n\nBuild in small steps: one component at a time, reading each answer before the next. A change the server refuses\nsays exactly what to fix.\n\nTry it the way a person arrives: `drive_page` from the app's start page (leave out `page`) and press through it,\nnot a page opened on its own.\n\nIf I ask for an editor, a viewer or a tool of my own that reads or changes an app here, the guide is the skill\n`nodegx-your-own-editor` (`.claude/skills/nodegx-your-own-editor/SKILL.md`). Read it first; any agent can.\n=== SKILLS ===\n/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/.claude/skills/nodegx-your-own-editor/SKILL.md\n", "durationMs": 14.70887497998774, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "cat /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/CLAUDE.md; echo \"=== SKILLS ===\"; find /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/.claude -type f", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
