n-error\ngp_login1.failure -> gp_said.run\ngp_signup1.error -> gp_said.in-error\ngp_signup1.failure -> gp_said.run\ngp_said.out-message -> gp_setMsgErr.value\ngp_said.out-said -> gp_setMsgErr.do\ngp_view.out-savedText -> gp_setMsgSaved.value\ngp_saveFn.done -> gp_setMsgSaved.do\ngp_view.out-removedText -> gp_setMsgRemoved.value\ngp_removeFn.done -> gp_setMsgRemoved.do\ngp_saveFn.done -> gp_changes.storageFetch\ngp_removeFn.done -> gp_changes.storageFetch\n", "durationMs": 37.33145794831216, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np=\"/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/app/components/Pages/Grownups/connections.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor c in d[\"connections\"]:\n    print(f'{c[\"fromId\"]}.{c[\"fromProperty\"]} -> {c[\"toId\"]}.{c[\"toProperty\"]}')\nEOF", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "4bf25a55-dfdd-42b4-8722-6c45b1368fb6", "sessionId": "25505b9f-a8ea-dd62-6b8d-be45f136b4b6", "turnId": "5093e3ac-9153-41c4-bc70-29af6171bbc2", "inputEntryId": null, "createdAt": 1792605379215, "updatedAt": 1792605379594, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "reasoning", "text": "Now I have a complete picture of the auth flow. Let me also check the Game/Stage 3D component to understand the offline concern (the stage is a Function that runs the 3D). And the engine.js briefly. Let me also check the `net.noodl.user.User` node — it's a runtime node. I should understand what it provides: `authenticated`, `roles`, `username`, `fetch`.\n\nLet me look at the Stage 3D component and the engine. Also let me check the `nodegx.security.json` again: signup public, GameChange find/get public, functions saveChange/removeChange role:grownup, claimGrownup authenticated.\n\nNow, the key question for the plan: how does a child sign in? Currently there's only a grownups page with sign-in/sign-up, and the first account becomes the grownup. There's no per-child account concept. The save is per-device in localStorage.\n\nThe feature: kids sign in online and keep their progress. Requirements:\n- Child signs in and finds their game on another device.\n- Players are children 8-13, no email. A grown-up sets them up.\n- Two children of same family share one device, each own progress.\n- Game works for someone who never signs in; a child with existing local progress must not lose it when they first sign in.\n- If connection drops mid-game, nothing lost.\n- Needs a backend and server-side workflows.\n\nSo the plan needs to design:\n1. A family/account model: grown-up account (already exists) creates child profiles. Children sign in with a username + PIN (no email). NodeGX has `net.noodl.user.SignUp`/`LogIn` which use username/password. So children could be accounts with username + password (a short PIN). But the requirement says \"a grown-up in the family should be the one who sets them up\" — so the grown-up creates the child account, or the child account is linked to the family.\n\nLet me think about what NodeGX supports. The `net.noodl.user.SignUp` node creates an account with username/password. `net.noodl.user.LogIn` logs in. `net.noodl.user.User` gives authenticated/roles/username. Roles exist (grownup). So we can create child accounts with a role 'child' and a family link.\n\nBut how does a grown-up create a child account without the child's email? NodeGX signup is username+password. The grown-up could create the account by entering a username and a PIN. But then the grown-up knows the child's password. That's acceptable for a family setting. Alternatively, the child signs up themselves with a username+PIN, and the grown-up approves/links.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The requirement: \"They don't have an email address of their own, and a grown-up in the family should be the one who sets them up.\" So the grown-up creates the child's sign-in. The child then signs in with a short username and PIN.\n\nNow, the save data. Currently the save is a JSON blob in localStorage under `gala-game-v2`, in the GlobalStore \"gala\" key \"save\". The save shape is defined in `game/save.js` (fresh/mend/nextSeason). The save is per-device.\n\nFor cloud progress, we need to store the save server-side, keyed by child account. The existing backend has a `GameChange` collection (grown-up settings, shared across the family/school). We'd add a `PlayerSave` collection (or `Progress`) keyed by user id, holding the save JSON + a revision/updatedAt.\n\nNow the tricky requirements:\n- Merge local progress into the account on first sign-in (don't lose it).\n- Offline: nothing lost if connection drops mid-game. So the save must keep being written locally (localStorage) and synced to the server when possible, with a queue/outbox and conflict resolution.\n- Two children on one device: each has their own save; the local store must be keyed per child, and the \"not signed in\" save must be separate.\n\nLet me think about the design carefully.\n\nCurrent architecture:\n- `gala` GlobalStore (persist: true, storageKey \"gala-game-v2\") holds `save`.\n- `ui` GlobalStore (persist: false) holds screen state.\n- Start Up: reads `gala.state` → `su_open` mends → writes back to `gala.save`.\n- Dispatcher: every press → `dispatch()` → new save → `dp_setSave` writes to `gala.save`.\n- Grown-ups' changes: `GameChange` collection, applied once at startup via `applyOnce`.\n\nSo the save is written on every action. That's the natural sync point.\n\nDesign for cloud progress:\n\nData model (server):\n- `Player` collection: one row per child. Fields: `familyId` (the grown-up's user id), `name` (display name), `userId` (the child's account id), `createdAt`. Actually the child's account is a NodeGX user; the Player row links the user to the family and holds the display name.\n- `Progress` collection: one row per child (or per child+slot). Fields: `userId`, `save` (the JSON blob), `rev` (monotonic revision), `updatedAt`, `deviceId` maybe. Permissions: creator owns; but children need to read/write their own. NodeGX security: `creatorOwns: true` default. We need a cloud function to read/write progress because the client can't be trusted and because we need merge logic. Actually the save is the child's own; but a child could tamper. For a kids' game, tamper-resistance is nice but not critical. Still, the existing pattern uses cloud functions for writes (saveChange). We should follow the same pattern: a cloud function `saveProgress` that validates and writes, and `loadProgress` that reads.\n\nHmm, but the requirement \"If the connection drops in the middle of a game, nothing the child did should be lost\" means we need local-first with a durable outbox. The simplest robust approach: keep writing to localStorage on every action (as now), and additionally push to the server debounced; on reconnect, push the latest. Since the save is a single blob (last-write-wins per child), and only one device is likely active at a time, last-write-wins with a revision counter is adequate. But two devices could be used (tablet + school laptop) — the requirement says \"find their game exactly where they left it, on another device\", implying sequential use, not simultaneous. So last-write-wins with a server revision and a \"which is newer\" check is fine. We should still handle the case where the server has a newer save than the local one (e.g., child played on tablet, then opens laptop): on sign-in, compare revisions/timestamps and take the newer, or merge.\n\nActually \"exactly where they left it\" — the save is a single blob; the newest wins. But if a child plays offline on the laptop and then the tablet has a newer save, we'd lose the laptop's offline play. We need a conflict policy. Options:\n- Last-write-wins by server timestamp, but keep a local \"unsynced\" flag: if local has unsynced changes, push them (overwriting server) — but that could clobber the other device's newer progress.\n- Better: treat the save as a document with a revision; on sign-in, if local rev < server rev and local has no unsynced changes, take server. If local has unsynced changes and server rev > local base rev, we have a conflict. For a kids' game, a reasonable policy: keep both — the server keeps the newer as the main save, and the local unsynced save is offered as a \"restore\" or merged. But merging two divergent saves is complex.\n\nGiven the scope (a plan, not implementation), I should propose a concrete, defensible policy and name the trade-off. I'll propose: per-child save document with a `rev`; local-first writes; a durable outbox in localStorage; on reconnect/sign-in, if the server's rev is ahead of the local base rev and the local outbox is non-empty, the server's save wins and the local one is kept aside as a \"recovered\" copy the grown-up can restore (or we do a field-level merge for the additive parts). Actually, let me think about what's mergeable: the save has `plan` (order, numbers, formations, costumes, hair, snack, parking, backdrop), `school` (stars, earned, owned, upgrades, furniture, name), `notebook`, `season`, `galaDone`, `seenIntro`, `lang`, `sound`, `seed`. Most of it is last-write-wins-ish. A field-level merge is possible but risky (e.g., stars spent). I'll propose last-write-wins with an explicit conflict rule and a \"keep the other copy\" safety net, and flag it as the main open question.\n\nHmm, but actually the requirement is more about: (a) sign in on another device and get your progress; (b) don't lose local progress on first sign-in; (c) don't lose anything if the connection drops. It doesn't explicitly require merging two divergent offline sessions. So I'll design for the common case and name the conflict case.\n\nNow, the \"first sign-in must not lose local progress\" requirement. Currently, a child plays without signing in; the save is in localStorage. When they first sign in, we must adopt that local save as their cloud save (if the account has no save yet), or merge. So: on first sign-in, if the account has no server save, upload the local save. If the account has a server save, compare and pick the newer (or ask). This is the \"claim\" step.\n\nTwo children on one device: the local save must be namespaced per child. Currently the storage key is fixed `gala-game-v2`. We need to change the storage key per signed-in child, e.g., `gala-game-v2:<userId>`, and keep the anonymous one as `gala-game-v2` (or `gala-game-v2:guest`). When a child signs in, we switch the store to their key. When they sign out, switch back to the guest key. This means the GlobalStore's `storageKey` must be dynamic — but NodeGX GlobalStore's storageKey is a parameter, likely fixed at build. Hmm. Let me check whether storageKey can be set at runtime.\n\nActually, the GlobalStore node has `storageKey` as a parameter. Can it be changed at runtime? Probably not via a wire (it's a parameter, not an input port). Let me check the node spec. I don't have the node-spec package installed. Let me check if node_modules exists.\n\nLet me check whether there's a node_modules with @nodegx packages, and whether I can query the node library. Actually the .mcp.json points to npx @nodegx/mcp. I could use the nodegx MCP tools, but I'm in headless mode and the tools aren't in my tool list. The AGENTS.md says to use `call_tool` if a tool isn't in my list. But I don't have a `call_tool` tool either. Hmm. Let me check if the nodegx MCP is available. Actually, my available tools are: skill, task, bash, edit, grep, read_file, todo, write_file. No MCP tools. So I can't call nodegx tools directly. But I could potentially run the MCP server via bash? That's complex. \n\nActually, for a plan, I don't strictly need to run the app. But it would help to know the GlobalStore node's ports. Let me check if there's a cached copy of the node library or the @nodegx packages anywhere.\n\nLet me search for node_modules and any nodegx package.\n\nActually, the task is to write a plan, not to build. I should be careful not to over-invest. But I want the plan to be accurate about NodeGX capabilities. Let me check if I can find the node spec for GlobalStore, User, SignUp, etc.\n\nLet me look for node_modules or any cached nodegx packages.", "summary": []}
{"id": "call_d37ef618937c4167a243a6b0", "sessionId": "25505b9f-a8ea-dd62-6b8d-be45f136b4b6", "turnId": "5093e3ac-9153-41c4-bc70-29af6171bbc2", "inputEntryId": null, "createdAt": 1792605379601, "updatedAt": 1792605379661, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "effect", "title": "bash", "detail": {"toolName": "bash", "display": {"summary": "bash: python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np=\"/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/app/components/Game/Stage 3D/nodes.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor n in d[\"nodes\"]:\n    print(\"###\", n[\"id\"], n[\"type\"], \"|\", n.get(\"label\",\"\"))\n    print(json.dumps(n.get(\"parameters\",{}), ensure_ascii=False)[:600])\n    print()\nEOF", "content": null, "suffix": "", "verb": "Running", "message": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np=\"/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/app/components/Game/Stage 3D/nodes.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor n in d[\"nodes\"]:\n    print(\"###\", n[\"id\"], n[\"type\"], \"|\", n.get(\"label\",\"\"))\n    print(json.dumps(n.get(\"parameters\",{}), ensure_ascii=False)[:600])\n    print()\nEOF", "settledVerb": "Ran", "settledMessage": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np=\"/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/app/components/Game/Stage 3D/nodes.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor n in d[\"nodes\"]:\n    print(\"###\", n[\"id\"], n[\"type\"], \"|\", n.get(\"label\",\"\"))\n    print(json.dumps(n.get(\"parameters\",{}), ensure_ascii=False)[:600])\n    print()\nEOF", "statusText": "Running command"}, "kind": "shell", "input": {"command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np=\"/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/app/components/Game/Stage 3D/nodes.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor n in d[\"nodes\"]:\n    print(\"###\", n[\"id\"], n[\"type\"], \"|\", n.get(\"label\",\"\"))\n    print(json.dumps(n.get(\"parameters\",{}), ensure_ascii=False)[:600])\n    print()\nEOF"}}, "state": {"status": "completed", "output": {"stdout": "### s3_in Component Inputs | \n{}\n\n### s3_out Component Outputs | \n{}\n\n### s3_host Group | 3D view\n{\"position\": \"absolute\", \"width\": {\"value\": 100, \"unit\": \"%\"}, \"height\": {\"value\": 100, \"unit\": \"%\"}, \"zIndex\": 0, \"backgroundColor\": \"var(--scene-sky)\", \"clip\": true}\n\n### s3_run JavaScriptFunction | 3D stage\n{\"uses\": \"stage/stage,stage/world,stage/people,stage/play,stage/music,rules/data,rules/engine,rules/tunes,game/text\", \"runOnChange-in-host\": false, \"runOnChange-in-save\": false, \"runOnChange-in-ui\": false, \"runOnChange-in-words\": false, \"scriptOutputs\": [{\"id\": \"stage\", \"label\": \"stage\"}, {\"id\": \"live\", \"label\": \"live\"}, {\"id\": \"liveChanged\", \"label\": \"liveChanged\"}, {\"id\": \"cam\", \"label\": \"cam\"}, {\"id\": \"camChanged\", \"label\": \"camChanged\"}, {\"id\": \"float\", \"label\": \"float\"}, {\"id\": \"floatChanged\", \"label\": \"floatChanged\"}, {\"id\": \"act\", \"label\": \"act\"}, {\"id\": \"arg\", \"label\": \"arg\"}, {\"id\": \"\n\n### s3_sync JavaScriptFunction | Tell the stage\n{\"uses\": \"game/text,rules/data\", \"functionScript\": \"if (!Inputs.stage || !Inputs.save) return;\\nconst w = Scripts.text.words(Inputs.words || [], Inputs.save.lang || 'fr');\\nInputs.stage.sync(Inputs.save, Inputs.ui || {}, (Inputs.save.school.name || '').trim() || w('school'));\\n\"}\n\n### s3_bye JavaScriptFunction | Stop the 3D when the page goes\n{\"runOnChange-in-stage\": false, \"functionScript\": \"if (Inputs.stage && Inputs.stage.unmount) Inputs.stage.unmount();\\n\"}\n\n### s3_live net.noodl.GlobalStore.Set | The evening so far\n{\"storeName\": \"ui\", \"key\": \"live\"}\n\n### s3_cam net.noodl.GlobalStore.Set | The camera\n{\"storeName\": \"ui\", \"key\": \"cam\"}\n\n### s3_float net.noodl.GlobalStore.Set | Where the toolbar goes\n{\"storeName\": \"ui\", \"key\": \"float\"}\n\n### s3_send Event Sender | A tap or the end of a run\n{\"channelName\": \"gala-act\", \"payload\": \"act,arg\"}\n\n", "stderr": "", "output": "", "truncated": false}, "outputText": "### s3_in Component Inputs | \n{}\n\n### s3_out Component Outputs | \n{}\n\n### s3_host Group | 3D view\n{\"position\": \"absolute\", \"width\": {\"value\": 100, \"unit\": \"%\"}, \"height\": {\"value\": 100, \"unit\": \"%\"}, \"zIndex\": 0, \"backgroundColor\": \"var(--scene-sky)\", \"clip\": true}\n\n### s3_run JavaScriptFunction | 3D stage\n{\"uses\": \"stage/stage,stage/world,stage/people,stage/play,stage/music,rules/data,rules/engine,rules/tunes,game/text\", \"runOnChange-in-host\": false, \"runOnChange-in-save\": false, \"runOnChange-in-ui\": false, \"runOnChange-in-words\": false, \"scriptOutputs\": [{\"id\": \"stage\", \"label\": \"stage\"}, {\"id\": \"live\", \"label\": \"live\"}, {\"id\": \"liveChanged\", \"label\": \"liveChanged\"}, {\"id\": \"cam\", \"label\": \"cam\"}, {\"id\": \"camChanged\", \"label\": \"camChanged\"}, {\"id\": \"float\", \"label\": \"float\"}, {\"id\": \"floatChanged\", \"label\": \"floatChanged\"}, {\"id\": \"act\", \"label\": \"act\"}, {\"id\": \"arg\", \"label\": \"arg\"}, {\"id\": \"\n\n### s3_sync JavaScriptFunction | Tell the stage\n{\"uses\": \"game/text,rules/data\", \"functionScript\": \"if (!Inputs.stage || !Inputs.save) return;\\nconst w = Scripts.text.words(Inputs.words || [], Inputs.save.lang || 'fr');\\nInputs.stage.sync(Inputs.save, Inputs.ui || {}, (Inputs.save.school.name || '').trim() || w('school'));\\n\"}\n\n### s3_bye JavaScriptFunction | Stop the 3D when the page goes\n{\"runOnChange-in-stage\": false, \"functionScript\": \"if (Inputs.stage && Inputs.stage.unmount) Inputs.stage.unmount();\\n\"}\n\n### s3_live net.noodl.GlobalStore.Set | The evening so far\n{\"storeName\": \"ui\", \"key\": \"live\"}\n\n### s3_cam net.noodl.GlobalStore.Set | The camera\n{\"storeName\": \"ui\", \"key\": \"cam\"}\n\n### s3_float net.noodl.GlobalStore.Set | Where the toolbar goes\n{\"storeName\": \"ui\", \"key\": \"float\"}\n\n### s3_send Event Sender | A tap or the end of a run\n{\"channelName\": \"gala-act\", \"payload\": \"act,arg\"}\n\n", "durationMs": 43.766875052824616, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np=\"/private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/app/components/Game/Stage 3D/nodes.json\"\nd=json.load(open(p))\nfor n in d[\"nodes\"]:\n    print(\"###\", n[\"id\"], n[\"type\"], \"|\", n.get(\"label\",\"\"))\n    print(json.dumps(n.get(\"parameters\",{}), ensure_ascii=False)[:600])\n    print()\nEOF", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
