ld check to know it works\n363:## 4. How I found my way around\n", "stderr": "", "output": "", "truncated": false}, "outputText": "-rw-r--r--@ 1 richardosborne  wheel  26609 Oct 21 20:05 /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/PLAN.md\n--- headings ---\n1:# Plan: children sign in and keep their progress\n12:## 1. How the game works today\n14:### What it is\n23:### How it is put together\n52:### The state: two Global Stores\n62:### The save\n76:### The loop\n85:### Boot\n102:### The backend today\n125:### Sign-in today\n142:### The parts this feature touches, named\n161:## 2. The plan\n163:### The shape of the change\n181:### Data to store, and where\n207:### Server-side workflows (new cloud functions)\n231:### How a child signs in\n248:### What happens to the progress already on the device\n261:### What happens offline\n277:### What could go wrong\n294:### Order of work\n316:## 3. What I would check to know it works\n363:## 4. How I found my way around\n", "durationMs": 39.9546658154577, "display": {"success": true, "verb": "Ran", "message": "ls -la /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/PLAN.md; echo \"--- headings ---\"; grep -n '^#' /private/var/tmp/own023-r3/B-vibe/work/gala/PLAN.md", "warnings": [], "approvalNote": null, "suffix": ""}, "decision": "execute", "approvalType": "always", "approvalSource": "bypass"}}
{"id": "fe5592e6-8e15-4c28-8395-f85b949e200e", "sessionId": "25505b9f-a8ea-dd62-6b8d-be45f136b4b6", "turnId": "5093e3ac-9153-41c4-bc70-29af6171bbc2", "inputEntryId": null, "createdAt": 1792605919146, "updatedAt": 1792605919256, "generationStatus": "completed", "relatedEntryId": null, "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`PLAN.md` is written (26 KB, four parts as asked). No other file was touched.\n\nWhat I found, in short:\n\n**The game** is *Le Gala de danse*, a NodeGX app — a folder of JSON, no server of its own. The player runs a dance school: programme, choreography, formations, costumes, dressing room, car park, then a simulated gala night. The whole game state is one **save** object, kept in a persisted Global Store (`gala`, `storageKey: \"gala-game-v2\"`) and rewritten on every button press through `Game/Dispatcher` → `game/dispatch.js`. Boot is `Logic/Start Up`, which mends the save and applies the grown-ups' changes fetched from the backend.\n\n**The backend already exists** — NodeGX cloud services with a `GameChange` collection and three cloud functions (`saveChange`, `removeChange`, `claimGrownup`), plus username/password sign-in on `Pages/Grownups`. But there is no notion of a child and no per-child progress.\n\n**The plan** adds a profile per child: a `saves` map and an `active` key beside the existing `save` (so nothing downstream changes), two new collections (`Player`, `Progress`) reached only through new cloud functions, a child sign-in page with username + PIN, and a local-first sync with optimistic concurrency. The existing device save migrates into the guest profile, so nothing is lost; the game never blocks on the network.\n\nTwo things I want to flag rather than bury:\n\n- The account model hinges on whether NodeGX can create a user account server-side. I planned for it and named two fallbacks, but step 1 of the work is to confirm it.\n- The `reference/src/` that `tools/sync-stage.mjs` generates the 3D stage from is **not in the folder**. The stage scripts are readable but not re-derivable — worth knowing before anyone touches them.\n\nPart 4 lists the rest of what I inferred from usage rather than documentation (the `net.noodl.user.*` ports, the `ui` store's shape, the boot order)."}], "source": null, "userDisplayContent": null}
